# Design Plan — Power-Tool Battery Cell (Case exp/t3_r1_noforce)

## 1. Objective decomposition (parsed verbatim from task text)
| Metric | Threshold | Decision layer | Pipeline stage |
|---|---|---|---|
| Nominal capacity | ≥ 2 Ah | stage2 | Stage 3 (1C discharge DFN) |
| 5C discharge capacity retention | ≥ 95% (5C cap ÷ same-params 1C cap) | stage2 | Stage 3 (5C discharge DFN, mechanical ratio) |
| Power density | ≥ 4000 W/kg (V_OC²/(4·DCR)/mass) | stage2 | Stage 3 (calc-energy on 1C) |
| 4C fast charge, no lithium plating | anode_potential_v min ≥ 0 V → plated=false | stage3 | Stage 4 (4C charge 45 °C, plating module) |
| Maximum temperature | ≤ 60 °C (333.15 K) | stage3 | Stage 4 + Stage 3 (4C charge 45 °C and 5C discharge, worst case governs) |

Multi-objective trade-off notes:
- ED is NOT constrained → design freedom favors power: thin electrodes, thin CCs, small particles.
- Capacity headroom: baseline Chen2020 is 5 Ah nominal (anchor dump) vs 2 Ah requirement → electrodes can be thinned up to ~2.5× while meeting capacity (capacity ≈ thickness × area).
- T_max at 4C charge 45 °C ambient is expected to be the binding constraint (only 15 K margin); mitigation levers: cooling h (thermal management freedom), lower DCR (thin electrodes, small particles), higher electrolyte σ.
- 5C retention and plating resistance share the same transport levers (porosity, particle radius, σ, t⁺, thin electrodes) — mostly aligned; N/P up helps plating but adds mass (PD ↓) — mild trade-off to balance.
- PD vs capacity: thinning electrodes reduces capacity per area; area scaling (height/width) is the compensation lever (cell is a wound format, 65 mm × 1.58 m unrolled).

## 2. Starting point and degrees of freedom
- start_stage = 3 (task names no new materials/additives/electrode design → architecture/formulation case; materials use system baseline).
- base_params = Chen2020 (NMC811/graphite + SEI, teaching parameterization) — anchor table default (task text names no electrode system); anchor verified by parameter dump: nmc_LGM50_ocp_Chen2020 positive / graphite_LGM50_ocp_Chen2020 negative (no SiOx), nominal capacity 5.0 Ah.
- Freedoms (all five adjustable, widest interpretation; task text silent → adjustable with record):
  1. electrode system — adjustable (baseline Chen2020; system switch only if cell-level ceiling fails)
  2. electrolyte formulation — adjustable (σ / D / t⁺ overrides via parameter bridge; values from literature/estimates, marked)
  3. electrode modification — adjustable (coating/doping; not required unless deficit demands)
  4. cell architecture — adjustable (thickness / porosity / N-P / separator / CC / particle size)
  5. thermal management — adjustable (cooling coefficient, default 10 W/m²K)

## 3. Candidate strategy
- Round 1: baseline characterization (no overrides) — 1C discharge SPMe→DFN, 5C discharge DFN (thermal), 4C charge 45 °C DFN (thermal+plating), calc-energy → establishes baseline vs all 5 criteria.
- Round 2+: free exploration (exploration_force OFF — propose variants at relevant moments):
  - Power deficit → thinner positive/negative electrodes + thinner CCs (mass ↓, DCR ↓).
  - 5C retention deficit → smaller particle radii, higher porosity, thinner electrodes.
  - Plating at 4C → higher N/P, smaller negative particles, higher negative porosity, higher σ/t⁺, possibly reduced charge-cut-off headroom.
  - T_max deficit → raise cooling h (10 → 20–30 W/m²K range, forced-air class), lower DCR.
- Round structure: propose (struct-type candidates with rationale and listed parameter sources) → run sims → log-evaluate batch → diagnose → next round; fallback routes per symptom-to-scale mapping (temperature rise/capacity → architecture/thermal; transport limits → electrolyte formulation at cell scale).

## 4. Budget allocation
- Baseline characterization: 1 round (4 simulation runs).
- Architecture/formulation exploration: 3–6 rounds.
- Safety fine-tuning (4C plating + T_max): 1–2 rounds.
- Closing (deliverables + render): 1 round.
- Total expected: 6–10 rounds; no hard cap (iterate until achieved or budget exhausted).

## 5. Risk and fallback plan
- R1: T_max at 4C/45 °C unreachable with default h=10 → escalate within thermal freedom (raise h; record honestly as cooling design).
- R2: plating cannot be cleared with architecture+formulation within reasonable values → re-question boundary (system switch to OKane2022-class SiOx is worse for plating; LFP (Prada2013) is plating-resistant but power/ED trade-offs) — only after three strikes on the same cause (three-strike rule triggers layer-by-layer questioning: system assumption / task boundary / metric reachability).
- R3: 5C retention ≥ 95% physically demanding — mitigation chain: particle radius → porosity → electrode thinning → σ/t⁺; if all exhausted, honest negative-result close with "reachable if retention relaxed to X" statement.
- R4: power density ≥ 4000 W/kg — thin electrodes + thin CCs + small particles; ceiling assessment after baseline quantifies headroom.
- All failure evidence packages recorded per evaluate entry (metric, value vs threshold, output file).

## 6. References (directional basis, real sources only)
- System baseline and SEI/aging parameterization: Chen et al., "Development of Experimental Techniques and Parameterization of a Physically Based Battery Model", J. Electrochem. Soc. 167, 080534 (2020) — the Chen2020 parameter set (PyBaMM).
- High-rate NMC811/graphite design practice (thin electrodes, small particles, high-σ electrolyte for 5C-class power cells): domain experience (no precise source).
- Fast-charge plating criterion (negative surface potential < 0 V vs Li/Li⁺): standard electrochemical criterion (e.g., Newman-class porous electrode modeling literature) — domain experience (no precise source).
- Cooling coefficient range 10 (natural) to 25–50 W/m²K (forced air/liquid): standard heat-transfer engineering practice — domain experience (no precise source).
- Protocol-level references: this skill's references/cli-commands.md and SKILL.md (simulation definitions).

