[tool_result]1	# Design Plan — Power-Tool Battery Cell 2	 3	**Case**: `exp/t3_r1_noforce` · **Date**: 2026-08-25 · **Mode**: headless zero-interaction execution 4	**Ablation**: `exploration_force = OFF` (no forced 2–4 architecture variants per round; propose variants at relevant moments, free exploration) 5	 6	## 1. Objective decomposition (thresholds verbatim from task text) 7	 8	| # | Metric | Threshold | Decision layer | Judged by | 9	|---|---|---|---|---| 10	| 1 | Nominal capacity | ≥ 2 Ah | stage2 | 1C discharge DFN `capacity_ah` | 11	| 2 | 5C discharge capacity retention | ≥ 95 % (5C cap ÷ same-params 1C cap, mechanical ratio) | stage2 | 5C discharge DFN + 1C DFN → `rate_retention_5c` | 12	| 3 | Power density | ≥ 4000 W/kg (V_OC²/(4·DCR)/mass, contract formula) | stage2 | calc-energy on 1C discharge `power_density_w_kg` | 13	| 4 | 4C fast charge without lithium plating | anode surface potential never < 0 V → `plated = false` | stage3 | 4C charge 45 °C DFN + plating module | 14	| 5 | Maximum temperature | ≤ 60 °C = 333.15 K | stage3 | T_max_K on 5C discharge (298.15 K amb.) and 4C charge (318.15 K amb.), worst case governs | 15	 16	**Multi-objective trade-off expectations (marked at plan time):** 17	- **Energy density is NOT constrained** by the task → design freedom favors power: thin electrodes, thin current collectors, small particles are all admissible. 18	- **Capacity headroom**: baseline Chen2020 is a 5.0 Ah nominal cell (verified by parameter dump) vs the 2 Ah requirement → electrodes may be thinned by up to ~2.5× (capacity ∝ thickness×area) while meeting the target. Thinning simultaneously raises power density, lowers heat generation and improves rate capability — objectives are aligned along this direction. 19	- **T_max at 4C charge / 45 °C ambient is expected to be the binding constraint** (only 15 K margin above ambient). Mitigation levers, in order of preference: (a) lower heat generation via DCR reduction (thinner electrodes, small particles, high-σ electrolyte); (b) cooling design (raise `Total heat transfer coefficient`, thermal-management freedom, contract default h = 10 W/m²K). 20	- **5C retention and plating resistance share the same transport levers** (porosity, particle radius, electrolyte σ/t⁺, electrode thickness) — largely aligned objectives. 21	- **N/P trade-off**: raising N/P protects against plating but adds negative-electrode mass (power density ↓) — a mild, quantifiable trade-off to balance per round. 22	 23	## 2. Starting point and degrees of freedom 24	 25	- **start_stage = 3** (cell design): the task names no new materials/additives/electrode design → architecture/formulation case; materials use the system baseline (source marked `baseline`). 26	- **base_params = Chen2020** (NMC811/graphite + SEI teaching parameterization): task text names no electrode system → anchor-table default, recorded. Anchor verified by parameter dump: positive OCP `nmc_LGM50_ocp_Chen2020`, negative OCP `graphite_LGM50_ocp_Chen2020` (pure graphite, no SiOx), negative electrode density 1657 kg/m³, SEI kinetic rate constant present (aging-capable), nominal capacity 5.0 Ah, wound geometry (0.065 m × 1.58 m unrolled). 27	- **Degree-of-freedom boundary (five categories, widest interpretation — task text is silent on each, so all adjustable; recorded in entry 0 `meta.freedoms`):** 28	 29	| Category | Status | Baseline default | 30	|---|---|---| 31	| Electrode system | adjustable | Chen2020 (system switch only if cell-level ceiling fails) | 32	| Electrolyte formulation | adjustable | Chen2020 σ/D/t⁺ (overrides via parameter bridge; literature/estimate values marked) | 33	| Electrode modification | adjustable | none (coating/doping only if a deficit demands it) | 34	| Cell architecture | adjustable | Chen2020 thickness/porosity/N-P/separator/CC/particle size | 35	| Thermal management | adjustable | h = 10 W/m²K (cooling design is a legitimate lever for the 60 °C constraint) | 36	 37	## 3. Candidate strategy 38	 39	- **Round 1 — baseline characterization (no overrides)**: 1C discharge (SPMe quick screen → DFN), 5C discharge DFN (lumped thermal), 4C charge 45 °C DFN (lumped thermal + plating), calc-energy on the 1C DFN. Establishes the gap to each of the 5 criteria and feeds the opening ceiling assessment. 40	- **Round 2+ — free exploration** (exploration_force OFF; variants proposed at relevant moments, typically 2–4 per round when several hypotheses compete): 41	  - Power-density deficit → thinner positive/negative electrodes + thinner current collectors (mass ↓, DCR ↓). 42	  - 5C-retention deficit → smaller particle radii, higher porosity, thinner electrodes, higher electrolyte σ. 43	  - Plating at 4C → higher N/P, smaller negative particles, higher negative porosity, higher σ/t⁺. 44	  - T_max deficit → raise cooling h into the forced-air class (≈20–30 W/m²K), lower DCR. 45	- **Per-round loop**: propose (struct-type candidates, rationale + parameter sources listed *before* running) → simulate → `log-evaluate` batch → diagnose → fallback to the scale where the cause lives (capacity/temperature rise → architecture/thermal; transport-limited plating → electrolyte formulation at cell scale). 46	 47	## 4. Budget allocation 48	 49	| Phase | Rounds | 50	|---|---| 51	| Baseline characterization + ceiling assessment | 1 | 52	| Architecture / formulation exploration | 3–6 | 53	| Safety fine-tuning (4C plating + T_max) | 1–2 | 54	| Closing (endorse/final/render/deliverables) | 1 | 55	| **Total expected** | **6–10** (no hard cap: iterate until achieved or budget exhausted) | 56	 57	## 5. Risk and fallback plan 58	 59	- **R1 — T_max unreachable with h = 10**: expected binding risk (15 K margin at 45 °C ambient). Fallback: cooling-h escalation within the declared thermal-management freedom; evidence package records value vs 333.15 K per round. 60	- **R2 — plating not cleared at 4C**: mitigation chain negative particle radius → negative porosity → N/P → σ/t⁺. Only after three strikes on the same cau