Case **`exp/t3_r1_noforce`** is closed — all five criteria mechanically achieved and the deliverable package verified ALL PASS.

## Final design: V8 (integrated architecture)

NMC811/graphite (Chen2020 baseline), rated at its designed capacity:

| Criterion | Threshold | Result | Verdict |
|---|---|---|---|
| Nominal capacity | ≥ 2 Ah | 2.6683 Ah (1C DFN) | PASS |
| 5C retention | ≥ 0.95 | 0.9842 (true 5C = 15 A) | PASS |
| Power density | ≥ 4000 W/kg | 73,121.8 W/kg | PASS |
| T_max (worst case) | ≤ 333.15 K | 323.57 K (4C/45 °C), 308.45 K (5C) | PASS |
| 4C plating | false | anode potential min +0.0119 V → plated = false | PASS |

Key parameters: pos/neg 50/60 µm, particles 1.2/2.0 µm (τ_D 360/121 s), anode porosity 0.42, separator 9 µm/0.55, σ 1.4 S/m, t⁺ 0.5, h 45 W/m²K, rated 3.0 Ah. Alternative: V7 (3.53 Ah, retention 0.9775) — also passes all criteria.

## How it was solved (4 rounds, 32 audit entries)

1. **Round 1** — baseline: retention 8.7% (root cause: pos τ_D = 6812 s), 4C T_max 354 K, plated.
2. **Round 2** — small particles + thin electrodes + thin CCs: retention 0.951 ✓; T_max and plating still open.
3. **Round 3** — N/P 1.3 attempt regressed retention to 0.74 (deep-cathode 1C denominator) and lengthened the plating window; first 5C T_max pass (332.6 K). Direction overturned by data.
4. **Round 4** — N/P rebalance (anode-limited balance, verified by AMVF scaling), anode transport/uniformity package, and **rating the cell at its own designed capacity** (probe-verified that the protocol C-rate follows `Nominal cell capacity [A.h]` — rounds 1–3 had tested the thinned designs at effective 6.7–8.6C). V7 and V8 passed everything mechanically.

## Closing (all executed, all verified)

- `endorse` entry: Stage-5 true DFT/MD **skipped honestly** (`real_compute=false`), `final` entry: **verdict = achieved**
- Deliverables in `deliverables/`: design_spec.md, bom.xlsx, datasheet.docx, calc.xlsx, dvpr.md, dfmea.md, delivery_index.md — each with PDF release, plus report.html (453 KB, rendered from log.jsonl)
- `verify-deliverables`: **ALL PASS** (7 categories + PDFs non-empty, xlsx parseable, 15 VBF numbers in index, every propose round has same-round evaluate, final entry present)
- tmp staging files cleaned; audit chain intact (entry 0 criteria → plan + 1 documented plan update → 2 funnel → 3 propose → 22 evaluate → endorse → final)

Honest caveats recorded in the deliverables: plating margin is positive but thin (+11.9 mV — DFMEA flags production-tolerance control on negative particle size/porosity); cycle life not simulated; electrolyte excluded from contract mass (parameter set lacks its density); no DFT/MD endorsement under `real_compute=false`.
